35,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"Based on my research, it seems our previous arrangements had extremes. Last year we were too fragmented, while the shared house left no room for personal space. We need a balance that keeps us together without feeling crowded.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"That is a very thoughtful observation, Mizuki. It is so important that we all feel we have a little space to breathe while still enjoying each other's company. Balance truly is the key to a peaceful trip.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Minato,,I found out some things! The inns have set times for meals and we'd all sleep in one room on futons. But the island houses only have one bathroom and the water might get cold. Which one sounds better?,"{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minato, thank you for sharing. Sleeping in one room sounds quite cozy, though the bathroom situation on the island seems a bit precarious. I wonder if the convenience of the facilities outweighs the charm of the location.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Midori,,"@Minato, thank you for the info! It sounds like a trade-off. I found that valley inns include meals in the price, whereas city beds are separate and can vary a lot. A single bill for a whole house might be simpler.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Midori, a single bill is efficient, but we must consider the environment. If we choose a town with a public bath and shops, we solve the bathroom issue @Minato mentioned and ensure everyone has a place to step away.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Midori"",""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Midori, a single bill for a house does sound very simple. However, I wonder if paying for meals separately might be kinder to those of us with smaller appetites, so no one feels they are paying for more than they need.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Minato,,I think a city room sounds nice because it has a door. But I'm worried about the island house if the water gets cold. I don't like it when the water is cold.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minato, I understand your concern. Regarding the travel, the island requires a ferry that takes up two full days of our trip. In contrast, the city is very accessible by train. I believe a shorter journey would be more relaxing.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Jonathan, that's a very important point about the travel time. @Shizue, I understand your point about meals, but I'm worried that separate costs can become unpredictable. A fixed, all-in rate would let us know exactly what to expect.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Jonathan"",""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@Jonathan, the time saved on travel is a strong argument for the city. If we combine that with a location that offers both shared spaces and the ability to step away, we avoid the extremes of previous years.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Midori, I understand your worry about unpredictability. However, if we choose a house let as a whole, the cost is fixed and fair for everyone, while we can still handle our meals individually to be mindful of each other.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Minato,,I like the idea of a city room because it has a door and no strict timetable. It sounds more relaxing than having to be at the table at a certain time. Does everyone else like that too?,"{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minato, I agree. A lack of a strict timetable and a shorter journey would allow us to truly unwind. The city seems to offer the most peace and the least amount of stress regarding our schedule.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Minato, @Jonathan, the city does sound very relaxing and flexible. @Shizue, if a whole house in the city is an option with a fixed price, that would be perfect. It gives us the predictability I'm hoping for!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Minato"",""Jonathan"",""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,"It seems we have reached a consensus. The city option provides the logistical ease Jonathan wants, the flexibility Minato prefers, and the budget predictability Midori seeks, all while ensuring the personal space I believe is necessary for our group's harmony.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Jonathan"",""Minato"",""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Shizue,,It sounds as though we have found a wonderful solution that makes everyone happy. A city stay will be gentle on our time and our spirits. I am glad we could all be so considerate of one another.,"{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Minato,,I'm so happy we all agree! A city room with a door and no strict times sounds very cozy and peaceful. I can't wait to go on this trip with everyone!,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,I am glad we have found a path that prioritizes ease and tranquility. Minimizing the time spent in transit will allow us to return home feeling truly refreshed. I look forward to it.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Midori,,I'm so glad we've found a way to balance everything! A city stay sounds like a wonderful choice that respects everyone's needs. I'm really looking forward to a relaxing trip with all of you!,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
